  "solution": {
    "text": "(1) Saline hydrides are ionic hydrides such as <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>.</mo></math> When reacting with water to form a Base and hydrogen gas.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MH</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>MOH</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><br />(2) <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> when reacts with <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> produces <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br />(3) &nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0068_ae0b000b3b06.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 84px;\" /><br /><br />(4) Molecular hydrides are also called covalent hydrides. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HF</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> are covalent or molecular hydrides.<br /><br />Hence, all statements are correct."
